      "path": "src/coordinators/daily-review/daily-review.ts",
      "content": "A partially covered range loses all of its covered sessions here. `sessionsBetween` returns `NotCovered` as soon as any date is outside coverage, so a still-open Trade whose first exposure predates the calendar (with no earlier saved Action) makes `day.missed` empty even when many sessions before the Review Date are covered and unreviewed. Skip only the uncovered portion or constrain the range to calendar coverage before enumerating it, and add a boundary regression test.",
      "existing_code": "  const found = read.sessionDatesBetween(from, to);\n  return found.kind === 'Sessions' ? found.dates : [];",
      "start_line": 157,
      "end_line": 158,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/coordinators/daily-review/daily-review.ts",
      "content": "An absent earlier valuation does not necessarily mean the Trade was not yet open. At the start of calendar coverage, `read.previousSessionDate` is absent, so `eligibleTrades` leaves `before` undefined even for Trades held before the Review Date. This branch then reports their entire lifetime P\u0026L as today's change. Distinguish a genuinely not-yet-open Trade from a missing previous session/valuation, and return `Unavailable` for the latter.",
      "existing_code": "    if (earlier === undefined || earlier.kind === 'NotApplicable') change = change.add(now.value);",
      "start_line": 143,
      "end_line": 143,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
